Index local music files into the database

Usage: index [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --from <FROM>
          Start letter filter (a-z)
  -t, --to <TO>
          End letter filter (a-z)
  -o, --only <ONLY>
          Only process these artist folders (semicolon-separated)
      --folders <FOLDERS>
          Only index these exact folder paths relative to MUSIC_DIR (semicolon-separated)
      --release <RELEASE>
          Re-index a single release by its LocalRelease ID
      --overwrite
          Re-index all tracks, ignoring change detection
      --overwrite-with-images
          Re-index all tracks AND re-extract all cover art
      --prune
          Delete DB rows for files missing on disk even when most of the folder changed (bypasses the mount-blip ratio guard)
      --exact
          Exact match for --only (no prefix matching)
      --inspect
          Re-check existing files for metadata changes (size/mtime/hash comparison)
      --skip-covers
          Skip cover art extraction
      --resume
          Resume from last saved checkpoint
      --threads <THREADS>
          Rayon thread count for parallel extraction [default: 8]
      --music-dir <MUSIC_DIR>
          Override MUSIC_DIR from env
      --web
          Emit PROGRESS:{json} lines for the web terminal (default: pretty console)
      --emit-artist-ids <EMIT_ARTIST_IDS>
          Write processed artist IDs to file (one per line, used by refresh)
      --resolve-artists
          Only resolve artist tags against MusicBrainz and rebuild links, then exit (no folder scan)
      --dry-run
          With --resolve-artists: print the decisions without writing anything
      --skip-resolve
          Skip the end-of-run artist resolution pass
      --canonicalize-artists
          Only reconcile Artist rows with MusicBrainz (clear contradicted ids, rename to the canonical name, connect duplicates, sweep orphans), then exit. No network, no folder scan
  -h, --help
          Print help
